+**libSQL vector-index schema from `sqld` is not openable in Turso Database.**
+A SQLite-format file produced by libSQL server (`sqld`) or embedded libSQL that
+contains `CREATE INDEX ... ON ... (libsql_vector_idx(...))`, together with the
+associated `libsql_vector_meta_shadow` and `<index>_shadow` objects, keeps its
+application table and vector blob columns readable in stock SQLite, but
+`PRAGMA integrity_check` and `.dump` reimport fail there because
+`libsql_vector_idx()` is unknown. Turso Database refuses to open the whole file
+with `invalid expression in CREATE INDEX: libsql_vector_idx (...)`. This is a
+cross-engine schema-portability gap, not evidence of data corruption. Removing
+the vector index and its shadow objects restores a conventional SQLite file.
+Independent reproduction:
+https://github.com/withnative/libsql-vector-portability-evidence/tree/93b27f23960aeca6a19de17d02bc68684f2de93c.
+
